{
  "dom_id": "step-q106278",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)=(x-4)^{2}+19?$",
  "worked_solution": "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=4$ and $k=19,$ the vertex is $(4,19).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[19,\\infty ).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14228566/assets/59773154dbfb56f8ecd6dcd3f584ac31ffcdcf4b766f0b99fd6c8ae4ae73dd5f.png)",
